.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Converts an \fBIModelTool<T>\fP definition into a backend‑specific function object that can be exposed to an \fBAI\fP model\&. 

A factory implementing \fBIAIFunctionFactory<T, TAITOOL>\fP is used by model backends to translate internal tool definitions into the concrete function format required by the underlying \fBAI\fP runtime\&. 
.br
 This enables consistent tool‑exposure across different model backends, runtimes, and execution environments\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The prompt type used by the model backend\&. 
.br
\fITAITOOL\fP The backend‑specific function type produced by the factory\&. 
.RE
.PP

